# The signal: flag sixteen on the wreck.
dialogue signal
  node down narrator "I haul down number fifteen and fold it the way you'd fold a letter. Then I bend number sixteen on to the halyard."
    -> up
  node up narrator "It goes up in jerks, hand over hand, and breaks out at the masthead: shirts, patches, an L. A colour my mother would have hated."
    -> wait
  node wait quill "There. Now we wait for the captain to decide we're not dead."
    -> about
  node about narrator "A long way out past the reef, a ship comes about. The Marrow, lining up on the Old Nail, coming in through the Needle as if she's done it all her life."
    > "She's coming in." -> boats
    > "(Take Quill's hand.)" if aff >= 12 -> hand
  node hand narrator "Quill's hand is already there. Neither of us mentions it. We're busy watching the ship."
    -> boats
  node boats narrator "On the lagoon, a hundred and thirty sailors row for her in everything that floats. Somewhere among them my father is shouting the stroke, wrongly."
    -> cutter
  node cutter narrator "And across the water a grey cutter with a cloud on her sail slips her cable and runs for Port Vela with every stitch she owns."
    -> home
  node home quill "That's Cray's. He's running home to write us all down as lost."
    > "Let him try. I have better handwriting." -> END
      act 3
    > "Then we'll just have to get there first." -> END
      act 3
